# [ST09-I S5.7-3b] Is a certified execution admission STILL live?
# The selector (certifier side) owns the verdict; the pure executor
# only refuses on it. Covers the verify -> execute window: peer
# restart (selection lost), superseded certificate, identity change,
# map regression/staleness, and corridor-affecting map advance.
string route_digest
string certification_id
uint64 admission_map_revision
string scene_revision
# [ST09-I S5.7-6] per-leg scope (empty = route-level claim only). The
# leg must be one of the certified route's legs AND its certified
# load-state index must match the claim: the carrying phase authorizes
# pre-release legs, the unloaded phase the post-release retreat — a
# carrying scope never authorizes a post-release leg, and the release
# boundary (vacuum-off attachment digest change) is never misread as
# an identity change.
string leg_digest
string leg_load_state
---
bool live
string reason_code
string detail
